# Operator keys installed as /home/hamsci/.ssh/authorized_keys on every
# decoder VM built from the golden image (provision-components.sh copies this
# file verbatim).  hamsci has NOPASSWD sudo, so a key here is root on every
# station built from the resulting image.
#
# POLICY — rob, 2026-09-22: PERSONAL KEYS ONLY.
# This is the fallback door for when the guest agent is down and the console
# is 400 miles away.  It is not a general access-grant mechanism.
#
#   - rob's own machines: yes.
#   - a role or shared key (wsprdaemon@WD0 was offered and DECLINED): no.
#     Anyone holding that private key would get root on the whole fleet, and
#     a shared key cannot be revoked for one holder.
#   - another operator: their OWN key, on its own line, so it can be
#     attributed and removed independently.
#
# ⚠ 2026-09-22: the BUILD RIG (root@192.168.1.182, /root/appliance/v3)
# carried a DIFFERENT rob.pub holding only rob@robinett.us, and it is not
# a git checkout, so it never saw this file.  Every decoder VM built there
# -- v3.48 through v3.50, AI6VN included -- answers to that key ALONE.
# It looked like the VMs were keyless; they were not, they had a key
# nobody was trying.  This file is now the union of all three, and the
# rig's copy is synced from it.  Diverge them again and the next lockout
# is the same lockout.
#
# Rotation is image-scoped: editing this file changes FUTURE golden VMs only.
# Stations already in the field keep whatever key their image shipped with.

ssh-rsa  rob@robs-macbookpro-at-home
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIK2CBQFokA4+Br6VXLVxs8GI6J1n4elqvCtlPpAyWcFs sigmond-devbox (rob)
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAINOhAVVLF/T6xVnMy7tZcsh51bYyAPX7NfPAzw5nEFYo rob@robinett.us (sigmond dev)
